WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:06.660
The last few months have seen remarkable progress
within the Regeneration East Area.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.879
A new bmx track has been designed and built
by Olympian, Trent Jones, and construction

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.280
is nearly complete with final planting and
grass to be established

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.200
before it opens for use.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.019
Directly opposite, the earthworks for the
sport fields are making good progress, and

00:00:22.019 --> 00:00:26.439
we’ll soon be able to start on the softball
pitches and changing room facilities.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.020
The storm water management area is also finished,

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:31.980
allowing the Honda forest planting to get underway.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.960
The first community planting day was held
in late May with nearly 700 native trees and

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.520
shrubs dug into their new home.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.480
The surrounding 3.2 hectares will gradually
be restored to lowland podocarp forest;

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.400
and interspersed with walking and cycling paths.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.560
And this has all been made possible by the
support of the Honda Treefund.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:58.140
This year we’re celebrating 30 years of
being in New Zealand and as part of that celebration,

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.400
we’re committed to planting 30,000 trees
in one year

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.280
and the Kaiapoi Regeneration project is part of that 30,000 trees.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:10.340
We’re really thrilled to be part of it and
we hope our customers will come out and share

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.080
in the forest and help plant it.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.080
Mayor David Ayers officially opened the Honda Forest

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:19.480
alongside Managing Director of Honda New Zealand, Nobuya Sonada.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:23.420
He says it was pleasing to see former residents
of the area, taking part.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:29.280
I hope they will come back here in future
years and say, "Well, my piece of land contributed

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.780
to something wonderful for Kaiapoi and Waimakariri
and for Canterbury."

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.200
And with over 14,000 trees yet to be planted,
there will be plenty more opportunities for

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.440
the community to take part in the restoration
of this area.

